# Research-lab threads

One folder per idea. Link related threads; do not merge them (`fep-paper` ↔ `voltmem-extensions` ↔ `licensing-collective-selves`).

| File | Role | Edit rule |
|---|---|---|
| `README.md` | Rewriteable snapshot | Current state only. Empty `Core question / thesis` means formulate — do not invent a thesis. |
| `log.md` | Dated journal | Append; never rewrite history. |
| `refs.md` | Informal sources | Full citation only if it graduates to a paper. |
| `notes/` | Trail, drafts, figures | Durable working prose when the root would get noisy. |
| `scratch/` | Experiments | Disposable; not the record. |

Root [README.md](README.md) is the lab index. Idea READMEs are snapshots.

## Do not mix roles

- Dated moves go in `log.md`, not the snapshot.
- Mechanism, mapping, and thesis live in the snapshot and/or `notes/` — not in the log or `refs.md`.
- `refs.md` lists sources; it is not the argument.

```markdown
# Bad — diary in the snapshot
## 2026-09-22
- Moved drafts to notes/

# Good — rewrite snapshot; append log
## Core question / thesis
Logical vs psychological novelty are two exits of one compression process.
```
